# Abuse of an email platform, with the messaging pack acting.
# Story 1: a new account imports four addresses, one per big mailbox provider:
# an inbox placement probe from a fresh, unpaid account. It is quarantined.
# Story 2: sends to addresses that look like the sender's own, a send right
# after an import, a burst of sends, a burst of test sends.
# Story 3: bad imported lists: role addresses (the application sends the list
# shape), throwaway domains, addresses that bounced before. A reviewed account
# that sends afterwards is risky.
# Control: a paying organiser, 30 days old, imports a list and sends a campaign.
# packs: messaging
# enforce
# list: disposable_domains tempmail.example
# Story 1: the probe
{"event": {"id": "ending-1", "type": "account.created", "at": "2026-10-19T08:00:00Z", "actor_id": "probe_1", "email": "probe1@example.com", "ip": "198.18.1.1", "country": "BE"}}
{"event": {"id": "ending-2", "type": "message.contacts_imported", "at": "2026-10-19T08:20:00Z", "actor_id": "probe_1", "email": "probe1@example.com", "ip": "198.18.1.1", "country": "BE", "attrs": {"count": 4, "recipients": ["one.test@gmail.com", "two.test@yahoo.com", "three.test@outlook.com", "four.test@icloud.com"]}}, "expect": {"decision": "quarantine", "status": "quarantined", "rules": ["msg_inbox_probe", "msg_fresh_account", "msg_very_fresh_account", "msg_untrusted"], "actions": ["quarantine"]}}
